{
  "case_id": "2016-16-254",
  "document_hash": "db154d196f142a5c0c1949fe9c8194009f74b5ee42aac6dd2caa15405b4e3775",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Supreme Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-254",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db154d196f142a5c0c1949fe9c8194009f74b5ee42aac6dd2caa15405b4e3775",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db154d196f14-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:22 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-16-254",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db154d196f142a5c0c1949fe9c8194009f74b5ee42aac6dd2caa15405b4e3775",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db154d196f14-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "At issue in this case is whether The Hague Service Convention permits service of process by mail if the State of destination does not object. Our position is that such mail service is allowed, and it's a three-part argument."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-16-254",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db154d196f142a5c0c1949fe9c8194009f74b5ee42aac6dd2caa15405b4e3775",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db154d196f14-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, purely textual evidence of meaning shows that this reading of the treaty is at least reasonable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-254",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db154d196f142a5c0c1949fe9c8194009f74b5ee42aac6dd2caa15405b4e3775",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db154d196f14-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you agree with that proposition?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States, as amicus curiae",
      "case_id": "2016-16-254",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db154d196f142a5c0c1949fe9c8194009f74b5ee42aac6dd2caa15405b4e3775",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db154d196f14-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Article 10(a) of the Hague Service Convention permits service through postal channels on persons abroad if the law of the forum State -- that's the State where the case is pending -- authorizes such service and if the receiving State where the mail will be delivered hasn't objected to Article 10(a)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-16-254",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "db154d196f142a5c0c1949fe9c8194009f74b5ee42aac6dd2caa15405b4e3775",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db154d196f14-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is it a convention on the service of documents? It's not a convention about sending documents, but it's a convention -- everything in this convention relates to service, and the whole purpose of it was to facilitate international cooperation in litigation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hootman",
      "case_id": "2016-16-254",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "db154d196f142a5c0c1949fe9c8194009f74b5ee42aac6dd2caa15405b4e3775",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db154d196f14-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I do not think that there is an ambiguity in -- in this particular point that we're all here talking about."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-16-254",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "db154d196f142a5c0c1949fe9c8194009f74b5ee42aac6dd2caa15405b4e3775",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db154d196f14-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm -- I'm not grasping what you mean by \"process.\" It's on the -- the convention is on the service of documents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-254",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "db154d196f142a5c0c1949fe9c8194009f74b5ee42aac6dd2caa15405b4e3775",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db154d196f14-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I'm sorry. Did we give up or do you think they thought we were giving up the right to authorize States to permit service by mail?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-16-254",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "db154d196f142a5c0c1949fe9c8194009f74b5ee42aac6dd2caa15405b4e3775",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db154d196f14-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, if it's -- if it's permitted under a Federal treaty, then how can Texas not permit it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-254",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "db154d196f142a5c0c1949fe9c8194009f74b5ee42aac6dd2caa15405b4e3775",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db154d196f14-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So why wasn't the service here pursuant to one of those authorized Texas ways?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-254",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "db154d196f142a5c0c1949fe9c8194009f74b5ee42aac6dd2caa15405b4e3775",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db154d196f14-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you think it's a problem for your position that no other court in the world has construed the treaty this way?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-254",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "db154d196f142a5c0c1949fe9c8194009f74b5ee42aac6dd2caa15405b4e3775",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db154d196f14-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, one question I suppose might be whether that is in fact producing the disparity in -- in judgments."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-254",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db154d196f142a5c0c1949fe9c8194009f74b5ee42aac6dd2caa15405b4e3775",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db154d196f14-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Sotomayor: Mr. Gaston, would you start with the Brockmeyer question? Do you agree with the government on the issue that the treaty only permits, doesn't necessarily authorize? And then your adversary's position that the Texas court has already said that under Texas law, you can't serve this way."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-16-254",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db154d196f142a5c0c1949fe9c8194009f74b5ee42aac6dd2caa15405b4e3775",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db154d196f14-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "States' position and it points out, actually, an ambiguity in the world \"authorize,\" which is the question presented that -- that -- that ambiguity is my responsibility, because \"authorized\" can mean empower or it can mean permit. And in this situation, permit is what the Brockmeyer case reads it as, it's what the United States suggests is correct, and we -- we think that is correct because of the ambiguity in the statute of what the freedom to do things means."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-254",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db154d196f142a5c0c1949fe9c8194009f74b5ee42aac6dd2caa15405b4e3775",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db154d196f14-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 12:13 p.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
    {
